<reference id="r_Image_Rasters">
  <title>Image Raster Formats</title>
  <shortdesc>A type of digital image that allows for photorealistic details, but loses quality when scaled.
  </shortdesc>
  <refbody>
    <!-- LINDGREN
      - <section> should not be used like a <p> paragraph.
        I revised it to indicate how section is used to create
        scope for a subset of information. Now, you could
        potentially create multiple sections, if needed.
      - Also, your copy did not take on your theme styles until
        I revised them with the appropriate tags.
    -->
    <section>
      <p>
        Image rasters are digital images composed of a grid of pixels. As raster graphics are scaled up, quality decreases because they are dependent on resolution. Sizing the image up or down will impact image quality.
      </p>

      <p>
        Raster image files are generally larger in size than vector graphic files.
      </p>
      <!-- LINDGREN
        - properties table makes sense here, since it would
          briefly help explain these file formats.
        - As is, you would simply need a list
      -->
      <simpletable>
        <sthead>
          <stentry>Common raster file formats:</stentry>
        </sthead>
        <strow>
          <stentry>JPEG</stentry>
        </strow>
        <strow>
          <stentry>PNG</stentry>
        </strow>
        <strow>
          <stentry>GIF</stentry>
        </strow>
        <strow>
          <stentry>PSD</stentry>
        </strow>
      </simpletable>

    </section>
  </refbody>
</reference>